What's the correct weekYear? moment's weekYear = the year of the week that the date belongs to. For 2016-01-01 (Friday), in en-gb (dow=1, doy=4), week() = 53 and weekYear = 2015. So the week belongs to 2015.

The current implementation: `if (weekOfYear === 1 && month === 11) return year + 1; return year`. For 2016-01-01: week = 53, month = 0 → returns 2016. Wrong; should be 2015.

The correct implementation (upstream dayjs):
```js
export default (o, c) => {
  const proto = c.prototype
  proto.weekYear = function () {
    const month = this.month()
    const weekOfYear = this.week()
    const year = this.year()
    if (weekOfYear === 1 && month === 11) {
      return year + 1
    }
    if (month === 0 && weekOfYear >= 52) {
      return year - 1
    }
    return year
  }
}
```
